This is a plain text file with a .pdf extension, not real PDF bytes.
It exists specifically to test that the client-side PDF parser (pdf.js,
invoked via App.jsx's parsePDF()) fails gracefully instead of crashing when
handed a file that merely has a .pdf extension but isn't actually a PDF —
distinct from the server-side %PDF magic-number check already covered by
tests/security.test.js's "upload hardening — POST /api/parse-pdf" test,
which guards the API boundary rather than the client-side parse step.
